title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 2070 and inter_party_relationships_timer = 0;
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Europa.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The S&D cannot govern by itself. Because we do not have a majority, we need the support of other parties. Recently, our governments have consisted of the EPP and ESN. We must build a coalition to stop them, or perhaps we can stand alone.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the social-liberal Greens and euro-liberal Renew.
- @center: Pull the EPP away from the ESN.
- @left: Work towards repairing relationships with the Left.
- @spd_alone: The S&D can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@left
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; kpd_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: left_1 if blutmai = 0; left_2 if ideology == "girondins"; left_accelerated if accelerationism >= 50

@left_1
on-arrival: left_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if left_inter_party_seen <= 1; regulationist_dissent += 2; epp_relation -= 2; renew_relation -= 3; girondins_strength += 10

The left hopes that our ideology further aligns with us, and wishes to eventually reunite.

@left_2
on-arrival: left_relation += 10; regulationist_dissent += 1; renew_relation -= 1; girondins_strength += 5

The left is estatic for the victory of the moderate jacobins, and talks are already underway of a merger.

@left_accelerated
on-arrival: left_relation -=1; girondins_strength -= 5; resources += 1

The fall of the Left to accelerationism does not bode well for us, as we lose another ally against the accelerated. Hope falls.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; epp_relation += 2 if epp_party_leader == "Joos"
go-to: epp_op if epp_in_government = 1 and spd_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Brüning"; epp_coalition if spd_in_government = 1 and epp_in_government = 1; epp_bruning if chancellor = "Brüning"

@epp_op
on-arrival: epp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the EPP-led government, but that does not stop us from building bonds with the Christian Democrats.

@epp_coalition
on-arrival: epp_relation += 9*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations is a neccesity. [? if ideology == "neodemocrat": Their Christian Democrat faction appears to have some concrete edge over the party, they too, will become 'social democrats'. ?]


@epp_bruning
on-arrival: epp_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

The Brüning semi-autocratic regime makes building friendly relations marginally easier than in opposition, as we all have fear of the accelerated.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; greens_relation += 8
go-to: renew_hopeful if stresemann_dead = 0; renew_hopeless if stresemann_dead = 1 and year <= 1930; renew_moribund if year > 2071

The Greens have been an ambiguous partner over the course of Europa, but we can still trust they will pick us over the ESN. [? if ideology == "neodemocrat": Their social progressive faction appears to have some concrete edge over the party, they too, will become 'social democrats'. ?]


@renew_hopeful
on-arrival: renew_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

The euroliberals are always willing to accomodate us, even if their toleration for the ESN says otherwise.

@renew_hopeless
on-arrival: renew_relation += 4*(1 - dissent)

Renew Europe has been substansially weakened after the schism from the regionalists. They're not exactly willing to be friendly towards us, but we still make the effort.

Given the influence of Renew amongst Europa [? if president == "Hindenburg": and with President Hindenburg ?], it can still be helpful to appease them.

@renew_moribund
on-arrival: renew_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

Renew has been electorally moribund, so perhaps our efforts are best spent elsewhere. [? if ideology == "neodemocrat": Their Eurofederalist faction appears to have some concrete edge over the party, they too, will become 'social democrats'. ?]


@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment. [? if ideology == "neodemocrat": Nevertheless, the neodemocrats wishes to follow through with their plan for a bloc party. ?]

- @return: Continue...
